# Compiled output must never live in src/.
#
# A 2026-09-28 import commit ("Initial import: single-source-of-truth
# extraction") checked 166 tsc artifacts into src/ across these packages. The
# current tsconfig emits to dist/ (outDir "dist", rootDir "src"), so nothing
# regenerates them: they stayed frozen while the .ts sources moved on, leaving
# two versions of the same module side by side. 17 were provably stale.
#
# Not cosmetic. Vite's default resolve.extensions prefers .js over .ts, so a
# bundler walking src/ can load the stale copy while Next.js loads the live
# .ts. That is the WALLET_NETWORK_HEADER dual-store failure class, reproduced
# by the filesystem instead of by two stores -- and tsc/next build never see it.
#
# dist/ is deliberately NOT ignored: it is the tracked build output that
# package.json main/exports point at, and every consumer resolves there.
src/**/*.js
src/**/*.jsx
src/**/*.d.ts

# Installed dependencies are never part of the package repo.
node_modules/
